-- Q10882: S Corporations [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 1368(c)(2), when AAA is exhausted, distributions from an S corporation with accumulated C corporation E&P are treated as dividends to the extent of that E&P. Under Section 1(h)(11), these dividends from a domestic corporation qualify for the preferential qualified dividend rate (0%, 15%, or 20%).
Wrong (A): Return of basis applies only after both AAA and accumulated E&P are fully distributed. E&P takes priority over remaining stock basis under the ordering rules.
Wrong (B): The distribution is not treated as a capital gain because accumulated E&P has not been fully distributed. The dividend characterization takes precedence.
Wrong (D): The distribution is a qualified dividend taxed at preferential rates, not ordinary income taxed at marginal rates. The qualified dividend rate applies to dividends from domestic corporations.$EXPL$
