-- Q10884: S Corporations [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 1366(d)(2), losses suspended due to insufficient stock and debt basis carry forward only for the shareholder who incurred them and become deductible only when basis increases. Upon a complete disposition, the shareholder no longer holds the S corporation interest, and the $25,000 suspended loss is permanently disallowed.
Wrong (A): The sale does not restore basis for purposes of deducting suspended losses. The sale proceeds create capital gain, but the suspended operating loss requires stock or debt basis to become deductible.
Wrong (C): The suspended loss cannot offset the capital gain on the stock sale. These are separate items, and the suspended loss requires its own basis to be deductible.
Wrong (D): Suspended losses are personal to the shareholder who incurred them and do not transfer to a buyer of the stock.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 10884;

-- Q10885: S Corporations [easy/L2]
