  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 56(a)(3), taxpayers using the completed contract method must use the percentage-of-completion method for AMT. PCM income = 60% x ($2,000,000 - $1,400,000) = $360,000. Since CCM reports $0, the full $360,000 is a positive AMT adjustment.
