Wrong (B): The $840,000 represents 60% of total costs, which is not how PCM income is calculated. PCM income is based on completion percentage applied to total expected profit.
Wrong (C): The $600,000 represents total expected profit ($2,000,000 - $1,400,000). Only the 60% completion portion ($360,000) is recognized under PCM in this year.$EXPL$
